Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: LosslessCut
Upstream-Contact: Mikael Finstad <finstaden@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/mifi/lossless-cut
Comment:
 This package repackages upstream's official pre-built Linux application
 bundle rather than compiling from source. The bundle is an Electron
 application, so it embeds a copy of Electron, of the Chromium content
 runtime, and of FFmpeg. The stanzas below record the licences of those
 embedded components as well as of LosslessCut itself.
 .
 Upstream sells LosslessCut through the Mac App Store and the Microsoft
 Store and asks for donations, but states in its README that the program
 "will always remain free and open source". The source is GPL-2.0-only and
 the Linux builds are published publicly, so redistribution here is squarely
 within the licence.

Files: *
Copyright: 2016-2026 Mikael Finstad <finstaden@gmail.com>
License: GPL-2

Files: debian/*
Copyright: 2026 Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>
License: GPL-2

Files: LICENSE.electron.txt
Copyright: Electron contributors
           2013-2020 GitHub Inc.
License: Expat
Comment:
 Applies to the embedded Electron runtime, which is the losslesscut
 executable together with the .pak, .bin and locales data files.

Files: LICENSES.chromium.html
Copyright: The Chromium Authors and third-party contributors
License: BSD-3-clause and others
Comment:
 The embedded Chromium content runtime and its many third-party
 dependencies. Upstream ships the complete, generated licence disclosure as
 LICENSES.chromium.html; it is installed verbatim at
 /usr/lib/losslesscut/LICENSES.chromium.html and is the authoritative record
 for those components.

Files: resources/ffmpeg resources/ffprobe resources/libav* resources/libsw*
Copyright: 2000-2025 the FFmpeg developers
License: GPL-3+
Comment:
 The bundled FFmpeg 8.0 build is configured with --enable-gpl and
 --enable-version3, which makes the resulting binaries GPL-3.0 or later.
 Every codec is statically linked into these libraries, which therefore link
 against the C library alone. Note that LosslessCut's own code is
 GPL-2.0-only; the combination is upstream's own published arrangement, not
 one introduced by this packaging.

